<title>PAKISTAN: KARACHI PORT HANDLES 68,076 TONNES CARGO.</title>
<headline>KARACHI PORT HANDLES 68,076 TONNES CARGO.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 68,076 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday compared to 89,086 tonnes in the same period on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Friday	August 7</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 9,320	17,091</p>
<p>    Import cargo		58,756	71,995</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, five are expected to sail and four are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Sugar		  12,155	 Rong Jiang		8/8</p>
<p>Rock phosphate     27,000	 Philadelphia	    8/8</p>
<p>Vegetable oil	18,600	 Kristal		   Due</p>
<p>High speed diesel  51,000	 Warbah		    10/8</p>
<p>Crude oil	    65,000	 Capitan Miranda	 11/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom (9221) 5685192; Fax (9221) 5673428</p>
